    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2CHiDwgQt3zHhvwRCXabv3x)_\n\n**Before:** the top-level `README.org` only described the Arch Linux machines. Nothing in the repo said how I review, merge and resolve conflicts on the many AI-made PRs, or why.\n\n**After:** a new section \"Reviewing and merging AI-made changes on macOS\" in `README.org` (which is the repo's front page) with:\n- the stack: yadm, fish, SourceGit on the plain clone `~/src/dotfiles-test`, `gh` and the merge button, Forge and code-review (`sp-vcontrol`), `sp-magit-style`, and `emacs-pr` / `sp-sandbox`;\n- how `sp-vc-ai-workbench` fits (worktrees shared with Magit and SourceGit; it is still commented out in `init.el` and has never been loaded);\n- seven rules from the #18 to #22 stack: number-prefixed branches, merge on GitHub so PRs show Merged, no rebasing stacked branches after the parent merges, merge the parent into the child, keep both sides in `CHANGELOG.org`, mine/theirs, and trying a PR with `emacs-pr`;\n- a table of the alternatives (Graphite, git-branchless, jj, lazygit, GitKraken, Sublime Merge, Fork, Meld, VS Code merge editor, GitHub Desktop, Magit ediff, smerge-mode, consult-gh, magit-stack) with pros, cons and why SourceGit was chosen.\n\n`CHANGELOG.org` has an entry under Open pull requests.\n\n**Project files (to complete or correct this by hand):** the files Claude keeps for this project are in the project's shared folder, [open the project](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2). The ones this section draws on:\n- `yadm/sourcegit-merge-conflicts.md`: SourceGit merge and conflict steps, and what could not be verified\n- `yadm/stacked-pr-conflicts.md`: merge order for the stack, CHANGELOG conflicts, the squash-merged-parent case\n- `yadm/worktrees-with-magit.md` and `yadm/magit-merge-and-docs-branch.md`: worktrees and branch work on the yadm repo\n- `module-docs/review-guide.md`: Forge setup, token, and recipes for your own PRs with Magit and `gh`\n- `emacs-sandbox/emacs-pr.fish`: the sandbox function\n\n**Not verified:** I wrote this in a Linux container. No SourceGit button name, `gh` command, ediff wrapper or the workbench module was run on the Mac; tool details come from project docs and my own knowledge and untried items are marked /untested/ in the text. I could not confirm that `magit-stack` exists as a maintained package, and the table says so. The existing `CHANGELOG.org` already has repeated `** Changed` headings under Open pull requests from earlier conflict merges; I left them alone.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_015WpxMsqdEyLFUmgXrKUQvi",
